      "id": "claim_846e141943d34ea2a3b4582cbbfb5cb8",
      "statement": "The Makefile's build-windows target depends on build-web, runs go-winres make to bake Windows executable resources, and builds with GO_LDFLAGS injecting main.version/gitCommit/buildTime from `git describe --tags --always --dirty`, the short commit SHA, and the HEAD commit's ISO-8601 date.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L23-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba39088e7bef08873b86f365cabdf8431cd554984fbbe8918e064dfef2ab1ef6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13010f8636b74744bb30102e85eda9ea",
      "statement": "A local `make build` deliberately embeds `git describe --tags --always --dirty` (e.g. v0.3.3-21-g3664cac) rather than a bare release version, so a build behind the latest tag or built from uncommitted changes is visually distinguishable in the Hub's version display; this was added after a bug where develop had not merged main's latest tag and silently displayed a stale version.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L7-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a2ffb81727b364c1dede6987168daec7cf2c1130776f2e3d9abf66e6095f6a1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_08a6d0cfad9641f48a2045b4f8bba68d",
      "statement": "fmt-check/fmt delegate to scripts/check-gofmt.mjs rather than invoking gofmt directly in the Makefile, because that script needs to scope which files are checked and normalize CRLF before comparing, which a one-line Makefile rule cannot express.",
